# Valhalla routing engine. Server-side only.
#
# Note the missing VITE_ prefix: that is deliberate. Vite only inlines VITE_*
# variables into the client bundle, so these values never reach the browser.
# The browser talks to /api/isochrone and /api/route, which the dev server
# (and the Cloudflare Worker in production) forwards to this Valhalla
# instance with the costing model, walking speed and Richmond-area bounds
# fixed server-side.
#
# Self-hosting (the intended setup) is documented in valhalla/README.md.
# Once the Compose stack is running AND you have applied that README's
# max_contours edit to data/valhalla.json:
#
#   VALHALLA_URL=http://localhost:8002
#   VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS=60
#
# VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS must match the instance's
# service_limits.isochrone.max_contours; with 60 the whole 5-60 minute dial
# ladder is a single upstream query. Against a stock instance (limit 4)
# leave it unset and the proxy splits the ladder into chunks of 4. Setting
# it higher than the instance allows gets the whole batch rejected upstream.
#
# For evaluation only, FOSSGIS runs a public community instance. It is shared
# infrastructure, not a production dependency: fine for trying the app out,
# not something to leave under a public deployment.
#
#   VALHALLA_URL=https://valhalla1.openstreetmap.de
#   # leave VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS unset (stock limit of 4)
#
# For production: `npx wrangler deploy` reads VALHALLA_URL from wrangler.toml
# [vars], or set it as a secret if the URL itself should stay private.
VALHALLA_URL=
VALHALLA_MAX_CONTOURS=
